+## Stage 6 results (agent split6, tree split6, 2026-11-22)
+
+**Built, under `?split=1`.** Edits and view changes no longer re-solve everything whole. Under the split a solve
+keeps clusters and periods, solves an edit locally first, refines a reopened zone, and runs the T-2624 and T-3925
+paths, each the way one worker does. Flag off, nothing changed but `addParts`' zone order (below).
+
+**How the holders agree** (`demand.worker.ts` `run`, `factsOf`, `decide`, `agreeKeep`; protocol `Facts`, `ClusterFacts`):
+- One rule: no holder decides alone what a cluster keeps or solves locally. One holder solving a period another
+  keeps would wait for loads never sent.
+- **Before set-up** each holder sends every other solving worker, per cluster it holds some of (`facts`, key `pre`):
+  - whether its populations hold the cluster's `sig`, or would be kept within noise (T-1862)
+  - its `keptOf` mask
+  - the T-1733 facts: its touched zones and populations, whether its market part is intact, the touched and all
+    populations' pass ms per period, the periods its frozen populations hold a full trail of, and (the market's
+    holder) whether the window opens
+  - the T-1609 facts: its zones opened again, whether the rest are frozen, their trails
+- Every worker runs the same pure `decide` on the same list. A cluster is kept when every holder holds its sig,
+  kept by noise when every holder is within noise, else solved. The 35% share (T-3512) is the cluster's, over all
+  holders' passes. The local count in `plan` is the agreed one on every worker, so the page's "a worker with no local
+  stage" rule still holds.
+- **After set-up** the periods `set_network` kept are ANDed across a cluster's holders (`facts` key `keep:<k>`). A
+  period one holder kept and another did not is solved again by both.
+- The rough solve (stage 4) stays whole, with no agreement.
+
+**The local solve and refine under the split** (`localSolve`'s `hl`, `sendFrozen`, `heldLocal`):
+- **Who solves.** The holders whose populations the edit touched solve them, plus the market's holder when the
+  window opens. Every other holder of the cluster is frozen. It sends once, at the start, its populations' loads for
+  every round of every period solved (from their `trail`) and its riders coming. Then it sends its part of the local
+  result and is free. It never sets anything up, so a following edit's local solve still finds it intact.
+- **Each round**, a solving holder crowds on its own populations (frozen trails plus touched ones as they solve) plus
+  every other holder's. Those come from the frozen holders' sends and from the other solving holders after their
+  passes (loads tagged `local` or `refine`). The riders coming are added the same way (`come`). The market's holder
+  solves the window on the cluster's final loads and sends the result to the other solving holders (`window`) before
+  they cap.
+- With exact sums this is the same arithmetic as one worker's on-trail local solve. So local results equal one
+  worker's to the bit, as well as the finals, wherever the edit leaves the market's window shut. With the window
+  open they also came out equal in the Node check below.
+- One worker's fallback for populations with no full trail (the ended loads times `capRatio`) has no split form,
+  since `capRatio` is kept only by a worker holding the whole cluster. Under the split the holders then agree to
+  solve the cluster whole.
+- **Results.** Every holder sends a part of a cluster result (local, step, or a cluster done ahead), counted among
+  the cluster's holders; the final, among the active workers as before. The page's parts key now tells local and
+  step results apart from the cluster's whole one.
+- Not under the split: the free-flow preview after an edit (T-1533/T-1538, `noPreview` forced). Its estimate is per
+  worker and has no parts. So under the split a new line shows no figures until its cluster's first period lands
+  (T-2624 steps).
+
+**A zone order fix, flag on or off.** `addParts` added zones in the order of the parts, so `citySummary`'s keys came
+out by worker. A kind of day other than the weekday adds the zones' summaries in key order (`dayResult`). So the
+view's totals on the average day differed from one worker's in the last bit on all-China: rail trips 38,008,908.471873425
+against ...42. `addParts` now takes the registry order from the page (`cityAt`).
+
+**Checks.**
+- **Node, two split workers against one unsplit** (scratchpad `split6/pair.mjs`): the real worker, Boston on w0,
+  Philadelphia and the market on w1, and the page's relay and `addParts` played. 16 networks:
+  - a load with the barrier, and an edit at one level (periods kept)
+  - two clusters solved locally at once, a fare change and undo
+  - a network identical to the last (every cluster kept), a barrier solve again
+  - a level's trains switched off and on (the window opens: one `window` exchange each)
+  - Boston closed and opened again (refined, Philadelphia's holder frozen)
+  - two edits cut part way into their whole solves (T-3925)
+  
+  Every local result and every final, every period and field, equal to the bit. Also with the zones in the other
+  order, and with the share at 1%, where every edit goes whole.
+- **In the game** (play.mjs on my Vite 6123, saves loaded, scratchpad `split6/probe.js`, `chain2.sh`,
+  `compare.mjs`; Chrome on 4-5 cores from the ledger, other agents on 6-10 of 16). The chain: +1 train at high on the
+  line with the most stops, fares 10% dearer, the line with the fewest stops removed, undo, the first line's 3rd stop
+  dropped, undo, the fares back. `wait`ed to each final.
+  - The machine reports enough memory that both pools came out at 3-4 workers. So these timings compare like with
+    like, not the pools players get.
